//- Merged service page (Sonny's D1) — the emergency + water-damage drafts
//- combined into ONE page targeting both queries, killing the cannibalisation.
//- Copy is merged-and-expanded from the two real drySafe drafts (emergency +
//- water-damage restoration); packages/pricing trace to real drySafe figures.
//- Built on the service-page template; services.js gates it published:null.
//-
//- DESIGN PASS (redesign + polish): presentation restyled to the landing page's
//- design language (promo-style hero, advantages trust cards, experience-card
//- steps, reviews-style testimonial, real .accordion FAQ). COPY IS FROZEN —
//- every word below is unchanged from the content-complete revision; only
//- markup/structure and the two-tone H1 highlight are new. Trust-row points are
//- the brief's compliant set (no attendance/availability/experience/volume/
//- "certified" claims). CTAs use the shared +ctaPrimary/+ctaTrust mixins.
extends _service

prepend head
  - const slug = "emergency-water-damage-restoration-sydney"
  - const _meta = (typeof services !== 'undefined' ? services : []).find(function (p) { return p.slug === slug; }) || {}
  - const pageTitle = _meta.title
  - const pageDescription = _meta.description

block service-body
  //- Re-lookup in body scope so the FAQ loop gets the registry faq array.
  - var _svc = (typeof services !== 'undefined' ? services : []).find(function (p) { return p.slug === slug; }) || {}

  //- ── Hero (promo-style: ratings badge → two-tone H1 → lede → CTA) ──
  section.service-hero
    .service-hero__inner
      .google-ratings
        .rating(style="--star-rating: 5")
        img.google-ratings__icon(src="img/google-icon.svg", alt="Google")
        span.google-ratings__label Google Reviews — 5.0 Rating
      h1.service-hero__title Emergency Water Damage &amp; <span class="text-blue">Flood Restoration</span> in Sydney
      p.service-hero__lede When water is spreading through your home right now — a burst flexi-hose under the sink, a washing-machine hose that's let go, storm water through the roof, or flooding through the ground floor — it's an emergency, and the clock starts the moment it happens. drySafe handles emergency water damage restoration across Sydney, fully self-serve — you book and pay online, with no callback or quote to arrange first.
      .service-hero__cta
        +ctaPrimary('cta--hero', 'No callback to arrange')
        +ctaTrust

  //- ── Compliant trust row (advantages-style; brief's sanctioned points) ──
  //- "Secure Stripe checkout" is carried by the hero +ctaTrust line above, so
  //- it is intentionally NOT repeated here (3 cards).
  ul.service-trust
    li.service-trust__card
      span.service-trust__icon
        svg(width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg")
          path(d="M3 6.5 9 12l3-3.5" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
          path(d="M8 17h13M8 12h13M8 7h4" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round")
      span.service-trust__text Measured to the IICRC S500 dry standard
    li.service-trust__card
      span.service-trust__icon
        svg(width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg")
          path(d="M7 3h7l4 4v14H7z" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round")
          path(d="M14 3v4h4M10 13h5M10 16.5h5" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
      span.service-trust__text Documented for your insurer
    li.service-trust__card
      span.service-trust__icon
        svg(width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg")
          path(d="M12 3 4 6.5v5c0 4.4 3.2 7.6 8 9 4.8-1.4 8-4.6 8-9v-5z" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round")
          path(d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
      span.service-trust__text Self-serve — book online

  p.service-lead Water damage is rarely as contained as it looks. Within the first hours it soaks down through carpet into the underlay, wicks up the base of plasterboard walls, and tracks along the subfloor and into timber framing — well beyond the wet patch you can actually see. That hidden spread is what turns a manageable spill into warped boards, lifting skirting, odour and lasting structural repair. It's also why what happens in the first day counts for more than almost anything that comes later.

  //- ── What happens on an emergency job (experience-card steps) ──
  section.service-section.service-steps
    h2.service-section__title What happens on an emergency job
    p.service-section__intro Restoration done properly is a sequence, not a mop and a fan pointed at the damp. On a drySafe job it runs in order, and each step earns the next:
    .experience__grid
      .experience__card.service-step
        span.service-step__num 1
        p.service-step__text #[strong Assessment] — we map how far the water has actually travelled using moisture readings, and check the water category, so the plan matches the real spread rather than the surface.
      .experience__card.service-step
        span.service-step__num 2
        p.service-step__text #[strong Extraction] — the standing and absorbed water is drawn out of carpet, underlay and hard floors before drying starts, because you can't dry a room that's still holding water.
      .experience__card.service-step
        span.service-step__num 3
        p.service-step__text #[strong Drying] — high-velocity air movers push air across the wet materials while a dehumidifier pulls the released moisture out of the room, so the structure itself dries rather than just the surface skinning over.
      .experience__card.service-step
        span.service-step__num 4
        p.service-step__text #[strong Verified dry] — readings taken against the IICRC S500 dry standard confirm the home is genuinely back to normal, and the result is documented for your own records and your insurer.

  //- ── What's included (package cards) ──
  section.service-section.service-packages
    h2.service-section__title What's included
    p.service-section__intro Two levels, so the response scales to how deep the water went:
    .service-packages__grid
      .service-package.card.card-white.card-rounded
        p.service-package__text #[strong drySafe Basic] covers the emergency essentials: high-velocity air movers and a surface moisture assessment — enough to begin drying the affected materials and to see where the water has reached.
      .service-package.card.card-white.card-rounded
        p.service-package__text #[strong drySafe Care] adds dehumidification and full moisture analytics, tracking the dry-down through to a verified, documented result. It's the option when water has gone deep or reached materials that hold moisture and need measuring over days, not hours.

  //- ── Across Greater Sydney (area card) ──
  section.service-section.service-area
    .service-area__card
      span.service-area__icon
        svg(width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg")
          path(d="M12 21s7-5.5 7-11a7 7 0 1 0-14 0c0 5.5 7 11 7 11z" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round")
          circle(cx="12" cy="10" r="2.5" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.6")
      .service-area__body
        h2.service-section__title Across Greater Sydney
        p drySafe works throughout Greater Sydney — the City of Parramatta, Cumberland, Ryde and The Hills among the council areas covered. Booking is built to be simple: booked and paid for online, with no callback to arrange.

  //- ── What it costs (pricing card — figures unchanged, not amplified) ──
  section.service-section.service-pricing
    .service-pricing__card
      h2.service-section__title What it costs
      p A traditional water-damage response usually starts with a paid call-out — around #[strong $499] for someone to attend and quote before any work happens. drySafe replaces that step with a fixed online price: book and pay online from #[strong $302], with no assessment fee. Booking online instead of paying for a traditional call-out saves you nearly 40%.
      p.service-page__disclaimer *From-prices are per room and exclude GST, any after-hours surcharge and package upgrades. After-hours surcharges are calculated at the time of booking based on drySafe's business-hours schedule.
      .service-cta-row
        +ctaPrimary('')

  //- ── Proof: before/after + testimonial (accreditation dropped — footer carries logos) ──
  section.service-section.service-proof
    h2.service-section__title The work, and who stands behind it
    .service-page__ba
      figure.service-page__ba-item
        img(loading="lazy", src="img/ba3-carpet-before.jpg", alt="Water damage darkening the beige carpet down a Sydney apartment hallway before drying", width="810", height="1080")
        figcaption Before
      figure.service-page__ba-item
        img(loading="lazy", src="img/ba3-carpet-after.jpg", alt="drySafe air movers and a dehumidifier running on the same carpet to dry it out", width="810", height="1080")
        figcaption Drying in progress
    .service-testimonial.card.card-white.card-rounded
      .rating.service-testimonial__rating(style="--star-rating: 5;")
      blockquote.service-testimonial__quote
        p “The team arrived on time and the work was set up professionally and efficiently. Their friendly and polite manner left me with great impressions.”
        cite.service-testimonial__cite
          span.service-testimonial__ava(data-letter="E")
          span.service-testimonial__name Eddie Lee, Google review

  //- ── FAQ — single-column .accordion (no photo; heading matches the page) ──
  //- Uses the global .accordion (styled in accordion.scss — main.js accordion()
  //- wires the rows by class, no shared-file edits) with the SAME _svc.faq array
  //- that feeds the FAQPage JSON-LD in _service.pug, so the two can never drift.
  //- Heading uses .service-section__title so it's the same size as every other
  //- section heading on the page. Caret is inline (the #caret-down sprite is
  //- only included on index.pug, not the service layout).
  section.service-section.service-faq
    h2.service-section__title FAQ
    .accordion
      each item, i in (_svc.faq || [])
        .accordion-item.card.card-primary-outline
          .accordion-item__header
            h3.h4.accordion-item__title= item.q
            button.accordion-item__btn.btn.btn-small.btn-transparent(type="button", aria-expanded="false", aria-controls='svc-faq-item-' + i, id='svc-accordion-btn-' + i)
              span.sr-only Toggle answer
              svg.service-faq__caret(width="16", height="10", viewBox="0 0 16 10", fill="none", xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg")
                path(d="M1 1l7 7 7-7", stroke="currentColor", stroke-width="2", stroke-linecap="round", stroke-linejoin="round")
          .accordion-item__body(id='svc-faq-item-' + i, role="region", aria-labelledby='svc-accordion-btn-' + i)
            .h5= item.a
    .service-cta-row
      +ctaPrimary('')

  //- ── Related reading ──
  section.service-section.service-links
    h2.service-section__title Related reading
    ul.service-links__list
      li Soaked carpet is the most common water emergency — see our guide to #[a(href='/blog/wet-carpet-drying-guide') wet carpet drying: what to expect and how long it takes].
      li More about drySafe and how self-serve booking works: #[a(href='https://drysafe.sydney/') drysafe.sydney].

  //- ── Closing CTA band ──
  section.service-close
    p.service-close__text If water's coming through your Sydney home, drySafe is fully self-serve — the booking's done online in a few minutes, and proper drying is what draws the water back out of the materials themselves.
    .service-cta-row
      +ctaPrimary('')
